      "id": "2126253002751164494",
      "text": "One of the largest North American banks says 'The Bottom Is In' for commodities:\n\nCommodities ripping overnight in Asia with copper +4.8% and gold +3%. Physical market appears to be buckling despite one-way price action largely driven by financial flows. Where’s the cue ball going? Look at silver and platinum lease rates going absolutely vertical! Gold ETF flows have continued to be resilient with inventories >100Moz despite worst price action in over a decade (’08 -34%, 2011-15 -45%, current -34%). \n \nDXY also cooled off from week to 103.7 from last week’s 104.5 highs. Subsequently real rates slightly off the 2.8% highs we saw.\n \nOur favourite commodities here are gold, copper, and uranium. The bottom is in, real rates are moving back towards one, buckle up.",
